+# Source and license audit — unchanged-carrier receiver pilot
+
+Date: 16 September 2026. This audit covers material used by this lead; it is not a patent clearance or a claim that cited algorithms are novel.
+
+## Pinned project inputs
+
+| Input | Pin / hash | Use and status |
+|---|---|---|
+| NISHAN protected baseline | Git `f37e861dc02815adf1bebb3e1b45ff222dccf821` | Existing implementation and public fixture. No production file is modified. |
+| Shared synthetic source pack | Git `1148b8b`; per-PDF hashes in `sources/manifest.json` | Six project-generated PDFs, copied byte-for-byte from the coordinator worktree. Development/validation/confirmation split is retained. |
+| Existing unmarked source | SHA-256 `5b347ce904b224a0b33602b12b905d0534d7f626c7319cec960f8bf2e7ed5b06` | Non-blind reference. |
+| Existing marked PDF | SHA-256 `7f85ad7ae5d65334ad9d055a26af0b434c71980628747e74d017a6431c86e9e5` | Exact public-fixture row bytes; unchanged matched carrier. |
+| Historical physical files | Exact hashes in `preregistration.json` | Private development inputs outside Git. They are neither redistributed nor called unseen tests. |
+
+The source-pack generator writes original synthetic prose and geometric primitives with PyMuPDF. It incorporates no third-party document, font file, image, model, or dataset. This lead will not commit original user captures, private keys, private codebooks, or temporary marked PDFs.
+
+## Primary research sources
+
+| Primary source | Established result used here | Incorporation/license boundary |
+|---|---|---|
+| Gábor Tardos, [*Optimal probabilistic fingerprint codes*](https://www.renyi.hu/~tardos/fingerprint.pdf), STOC 2003 / JACM 2008 | Conditional Bernoulli code construction and innocent-score reasoning. | Citation and independent implementation already in the repository; no paper text or third-party code copied. |
+| Peter Meerwald and Teddy Furon, [*Towards Joint Decoding of Tardos Fingerprinting Codes*](https://arxiv.org/abs/1104.5616), 2011 | Continuous extracted values and compound-channel soft decoding are prior art. | Conceptual comparator only. This pilot's bounded signed statistic and conditional MGF are implemented locally; no author code or weights used. |
+| J. J. K. Ó Ruanaidh Pereira and Thierry Pun, [*Robust template matching for affine resistant image watermarks*](https://archive-ouverte.unige.ch/unige:47477), IEEE TIP 2000 | Watermark synchronization templates and affine recovery are established. | Citation only; the pilot does not copy an implementation or claim template synchronization as new. |
+| Eugene T. Lin, [*Video and Image Watermark Synchronization*](https://www.cerias.purdue.edu/apps/reports_and_papers/view/2858), Purdue dissertation, 2005 | Watermark structure and redundancy can support synchronization. | Citation only. |
+| Benjamin Mathon, Patrick Bas, François Cayre, and Benoît Macq, [*Impacts of watermarking security on Tardos-based fingerprinting*](https://research.dial.uclouvain.be/entities/publication/35e8ed6f-e4c7-4db1-a722-0494ec36fa8d), IEEE TIFS 2013 | Physical symbol estimation and fingerprinting security must be evaluated together. | Citation only. |
+
+These sources support the novelty boundary: global channel fitting, soft evidence, local warp estimation, and compound-channel decoding are established research directions. This lead measures a specific receiver on the existing NISHAN carrier; it does not assert a new general watermarking method.
+
+## Runtime dependencies already present
+
+No package was installed or upgraded. The read-only shared environment reports:
+
+| Package | Version | Distribution license metadata |
+|---|---:|---|
+| NumPy | 2.5.3 | BSD-3-Clause plus bundled permissive components |
+| SciPy | 1.18.1 | BSD-3-Clause; wheel metadata also enumerates bundled runtime components |
+| OpenCV headless | 5.0.0.93 | Apache-2.0 |
+| Pillow | 12.3.0 | MIT-CMU |
+| cryptography | 50.0.1 | Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause |
+| PyMuPDF | 1.28.2 | AGPL-3.0 or Artifex commercial license |
+
+The experiment calls these installed libraries. It does not vendor or redistribute their source/binaries. PyMuPDF's dual-license status is a deployment/legal-review item already present in the project; this research commit does not change it.
+
+## Missing, sealed, or non-incorporated artifacts
+
+- `__PRIVATE_HOME__/LEGACY_TRIAL_CAPTURE.jpeg` is reported available through the coordinator but remains sealed from this lead until the preregistration and candidate implementation/configuration hashes are committed. Its byte hash and metadata are intentionally not read here.
+- No matched unmarked physical photograph, printer model/settings, print scale, lighting record, distance/angle, or physical calibration target is available.
+- The first historical file is a phone scanner/enhancement output; the second is an ordinary camera image transferred through WhatsApp. Neither substitutes for the reserved WhatsApp-**document** original category.
+- No separately acquired ordinary-photo/scanner pair of the prospective capture is available. Those categories will remain separate and missing rather than inferred.
+- No independent private-key/codebook document set exists for this unchanged-bytes comparison. Source-pack confirmation varies content only and cannot establish independent-key replication.
+- No third-party model weights, external corpus, paid service, or public upload is used.
+
+## Reproducibility and claim boundary
+
+All safe source code, synthetic inputs, hashes, settings, complete score vectors, and failures will be committed. User images remain referenced only by local path and cryptographic digest. A recovered transplanted donor pattern is explicitly evidence of pattern copying, not source authenticity, ledger integrity, non-framing, or human culpability.
